  "id": "perceived-fraudulence-scale",
  "term": "Perceived Fraudulence Scale",
  "definition": "The Perceived Fraudulence Scale is a self-report assessment used in research to measure the impostor phenomenon, meaning feelings of being an intellectual or professional fraud despite evidence of success. It is one of several scales developed to assess trait impostorism.",
